    "english":  "The blue neytal blooms along the brackish creeks,\nwhere the water-fowls dive for silver fish in the gentle dawn.\nThe lord of the expansive maritime realm, whose chariot travels\nalong the edge of the foaming tides, swore eternal faith by the sea.\nCan the great ocean wash away a sacred promise made to a maiden?\nMy mother notices the paleness spreading over my skin,\nand the neighborhood maidens exchange knowing glances.\nLet him come swiftly to our fishing hamlet and ask for my hand,\nere gossip tarnishes the purity of our spotless love!",
